        "original_id": "0ceff1bb-57b5-5a03-85be-43db9068b05e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carolina, Puerto Rico; San Juan; Columbus; Lockbourne; Franklin County, Ohio; Puerto Rico; United States\n- Organizations: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport; Rickenbacker International Airport\n- People: Luis Muñoz Marín\n- Concepts: civil-military airports; international airports; public airports\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is a joint civil-military international airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Luis Muñoz Marín, Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is also known as Isla Verde International Airport or Aeropuerto Internacional de Isla Verde.\n- Rickenbacker International Airport is a civil-military public airport 10 miles south of downtown Columbus, near Lockbourne in southern Franklin County, Ohio, United States.",
